                <pb facs="0357" n="357" xml:id="pg357"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pike to Mr.
                            Seward</hi>.</head>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Extract.]</note>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States
                            Legation</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic">The
                            Hague</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-07-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 12, 1861</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have communicated to Baron de Zuylen, as
                    directed, your high appreciation of the course of his government on our domestic
                    affairs, as manifested and expressed in his reply to my predecessor’s
                    communication of the 8th of April last.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES S. PIKE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
